Neither the bootloader nor the UKIs will remain unchanged with time. Updates to
either systemd-boot or the kernel will trigger either a new EFI binary being
copied to the EFI system partition or a rebuild of the associated UKI. Every
time this happens, the respective files need to be resigned. To make this
happen, we will create a pacman hook to trigger signing of updated bootloader
executables and edit uki.conf to include signing of UKI files part of their
build process.

To make sure that both the pacman hook and the UKI config are working, we will
not sign anything manually but create the necessary files and then simulate an
update to the systemd package.
